+-   **When not to use:** When high generalization to unseen subjects is required without fine-tuning, or when SMPL parameters are not available.
 
 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** Proposed by Zhen Xu, Hujun Bao, and Xiaowei Zhou from the State Key Laboratory of CAD&CG, Zhejiang University [S1].
-*   **Paper:** "Learning Neural Volumetric Representations of Dynamic Humans in Minutes" (CVPR 2023) [S1].
-*   **History:** The method builds on prior work in neural radiance fields for humans (e.g., Neural Body [58]) and multiresolution hash encoding [48] [S1]. It addresses the slow convergence of per-scene optimization methods by introducing a part-based representation and 2D motion parameterization [S1].
-*   **Usage:** Used for creating volumetric videos of human performers for applications such as immersive telepresence, video games, and movie production [S1].
